# Day 76: Jenkins Project Security (Project-Based Matrix Authorization)

## 📋 Overview
This lab implements fine-grained, project-level role-based access control (RBAC) in Jenkins using the **Matrix Authorization Strategy** (`matrix-auth`) plugin. Instead of granting broad global job privileges across all pipelines, authorization is scoped strictly to the **`Packages`** job while preserving parent ACL inheritance and isolating other existing jobs.

* **Track:** 100 Days of DevOps — KodeKloud Engineer (76% Complete)
* **Completion Date:** November 19, 2026
* **Environment:** Stratos Datacenter (`jump-host` → `jenkins:8080`, Jenkins `2.541.2`)
* **Target Job:** `Packages`
* **Authorization Strategy:** `ProjectMatrixAuthorizationStrategy` with `InheritParentStrategy`

---

## 🎯 Access Control Matrix

| Principal | Global Permissions | `Packages` Job Permissions | Other Jobs |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **`admin`** | `Overall/Administer` | Inherited (`Administer`) | Inherited (`Administer`) |
| **`sam`** | `Overall/Read` | `Item.Build`, `Item.Configure`, `Item.Read` | None (Isolated) |
| **`rohan`** | `Overall/Read` | `Item.Build`, `Item.Cancel`, `Item.Configure`, `Item.Read`, `Run.Update`, `SCM.Tag` | None (Isolated) |

* **Inheritance Mode:** `Inherit permissions from parent ACL` (`org.jenkinsci.plugins.matrixauth.inheritance.InheritParentStrategy`)

